map of the libstdoc repository
==============================

libstdoc is a small, freestanding standard C library for Linux on
aarch64.  It is built and linked without any host C library: it
provides its own program entry point, its own system-call layer and
its own formatting engine, which is what makes the test programs a
complete demonstration of the library rather than a hosted build that
happens to contain it.

This document lists every entry in the repository and says what it is
for.  The documents listed at the end describe the larger pieces.


