assembly/ - the runtime in assembly
-----------------------------------

    start_aarch64.S   Program entry point.  The kernel enters _start
                      with argc, argv and envp on the stack; the file
                      clears the frame chain, calls main(argc, argv,
                      envp) and hands main's return value to
                      stdoc_sys_exit.  There are no constructors, no
                      ".init_array" walk and no atexit handling: the
                      freestanding startup path does not provide
                      them.  Documented in docs/io.
    syscall.S         The system-call trampoline.  It converts the
                      ordinary C calling convention into the Linux
                      aarch64 system-call convention (number in x8,
                      arguments in x0..x5, result in x0) with a single
                      "svc #0".  Documented in docs/io.


io/ - the input/output layer
----------------------------

    stdoc_io.h        The internal interface shared by this layer and
                      the platform layer.  Nothing in it is public
                      API.  It also defines STDOC_BUFFER_SIZE, the
                      size of a stream's staging buffer.
    file.c            The three standard streams (stdoc_stdin,
                      stdoc_stdout, stdoc_stderr) and the staging
                      logic: stdoc_stream_write, stdoc_stream_flush
                      and stdoc_stream_discard.  Documented in
                      docs/io.
    vfprintf.c        The formatting engine, stdoc_vfprintf.  Parser
                      and formatter live in one translation unit.
                      Documented in docs/formatting.
    printf.c          stdoc_printf: the stdoc_stdout wrapper around
                      stdoc_vfprintf.
    fprintf.c         stdoc_fprintf: the same for a given stream.
    syscall_linux.c   The operating-system wrappers
                      (stdoc_sys_write, stdoc_sys_read, stdoc_sys_close,
                      stdoc_sys_exit) and the only place where Linux
                      system-call numbers appear.  Documented in
                      docs/io.
    string.c          The internal helpers stdoc_strlen, stdoc_memcpy
                      and stdoc_memset, which exist so that the
                      library links with "-nostdlib" without taking
                      symbols from a host C library.


mem/ - dynamic memory
---------------------

    heap.c            The allocator: a static arena, first-fit block
                      allocation with splitting and merging, the safe
                      variants that terminate the process on a
                      detected fault, and the accounting the tests
                      assert on.  Documented in docs/heap.
    stdoc_mem.h       The internal header: STDOC_HEAP_SIZE and the
                      accounting queries.  It is not installed.


include/ - the public API
-------------------------

    libstdoc.h        The C header: the streams, stdoc_printf,
                      stdoc_fprintf and the dynamic memory functions
                      stdoc_malloc, stdoc_free, stdoc_malloc_safe and
                      stdoc_free_safe.  The comments in this file are
                      the contract of the library.  It depends only on
                      "<stdarg.h>" and "<stddef.h>", so it works in a
                      freestanding build.  Documented in
                      docs/formatting and docs/heap.
    libstdoc.hpp      The C++ entry point: it includes libstdoc.h
                      inside an "extern "C"" specification so the
                      symbols are not mangled.  No C++ runtime is
                      required.


etc/ - installed package metadata
---------------------------------

    libstdoc.pc.in        Template of the pkg-config file, filled in
                          at configure time with the chosen prefix.
    libstdoc-config.cmake.in
                          Template of the CMake package config, so a
                          consumer can "find_package(libstdoc)".


test/ - the test programs
-------------------------

    CMakeLists.txt    Builds the tests and registers them with CTest.
    index.c           The original smoke test (legacy: built without
                      "-Werror").
    index.cxx         The same source as a C++ program, proving the
                      header works from C++.  Built as a hosted
                      program (legacy: also without "-Werror").
    format.c          The formatting engine test; its golden file was
                      produced by a reference C library.
    errors.c          The failure paths of the formatted functions.
    heap.c            The allocator, its safe variants and the leak
                      accounting.
    heap_abort.c      The fail-fast paths: one scenario per run,
                      selected on the command line.
    expected-index.txt, expected-format.txt
                      Golden output the programs are compared with.
    CompareOutput.cmake
                      Compares a program's output and exit status
                      with a golden file.
    CheckFatal.cmake  Requires a program to end with the documented
                      fatal status 134.
    The whole directory is documented in docs/testing.


.github/ - automation
---------------------

    dependabot.yml    Keeps the GitHub Actions dependencies updated.
    workflows/codeql.yml
                      The CodeQL analysis workflow.  Neither file
                      takes part in the build: this repository builds
                      with no network access.


Top-level files
---------------

    README            Project overview, repository structure and the
                      license summary.  Points here for details.
    NEWS              Release notes; the newest release is first.
                      1.0.0-beta covers the history from the commit
                      "major changes" to the present tree.
    ChangeLog         States that Git holds the detailed history.
    AUTHORS           The project founder, maintainer and developer.
    LICENSE           Explains the three licenses the recipient may
                      choose from.
    LICENSES/         GPL-2.0.txt, LGPL-2.1.txt, Apache-2.0.txt and a
                      README that explains how the choice works.
    AGENTS.md         The conventions that govern changes to this
                      tree: C17, freestanding rules, style, the
                      priority of instructions.  Read it before
                      editing anything.


